Dear Poster of software, patches, bug reports,

please support the poor moderators of software archives and make their
live much easier:

 - PLEASE suggest an ARCHIVE NAME for your software if you post a new
   program, package, etc.

 - PLEASE include a REFERENCE to the original software if you post a
   patch, an upgrade, a bug report, etc.
   The reference should include:
    + the name of the newsgroup in which the original software was
      posted
    + the archive name (or name & version if there is no archive name)
      of the original software

 - PLEASE include PART NUMBERS for multi-part postings in the `Subject:'
   header and/or in the article body


The archive names, references and part numbers should be placed at the
top of the postings.
You should use pseudo-headers at the top of the article body (like in
comp.sources.{games|misc|unix|x}):
	Archive-name:
	Part:
	Patch-to:
	O-Patch-to: [official patch]
	Bug-to:
	...
Examples:
	Subject:	BAR can do everything, Part 1/9999

	Archive-name:	FOO
	Archive-name:	BAR/part7
	Archive-name:	BAR/patch3
	Archive-name:	FOO/patch5b
	Part:		08 of 15
	Patch-to:	FOO posted in comp.sources.misc
	Bug-to:		comp.sources.misc:FOO
	Upgrade-to:	1.2 -> 1.3 of comp.sources.unix:BAR
	Missing-to:	comp.sources.x:BAR (v99i077-82)


Thanks in advance.
You will help us (at least me :-) ) very much.

